# shell: desktop
# A drag between poses: press on a file, move onto a folder, release.
# Rows sort folders first, so row 0 is "sub", row 1 is "a.txt".
note PVS-032: a press alone must not move anything
press 200 136
wait 2
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/a.txt
note PVS-035/PVS-037: dragging onto a folder and releasing moves it there
move 200 129
move 200 116
wait 2
release 200 116
wait 20
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/sub/a.txt
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_script/a.txt

note PVS-038: Option-dragging copies instead of moving -- the original stays
press 200 136
move 200 129
move 200 116
release 200 116 1 alt
wait 20
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/sub/b.txt
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/b.txt

note FS-003: a secondary-button drop offers Move/Copy/Link and obeys the pick
press 200 156 3
move 200 144 3
move 200 116 3
release 200 116 3
wait 3
menu-pick Move here
wait 25
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/sub/c.txt
note and Move is what it obeyed: a copy or a link would leave the source
expect-no-file /tmp/trk_script/c.txt
note PVS-051: a drag resting on a folder springs it open
press 200 136
move 200 129
move 200 116
wait 60
expect-title sub
note PVS-056: moving off the target drops the highlight, and the drop is
note then on nothing rather than on the folder it used to be over
move 700 500
release 700 500
wait 20
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/b.txt
quit
